{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "ChemVerticalMixing",
  "description": "Vertical mixing of chemical species in WRF-Chem, with the dry-deposition surface flux: SUBROUTINE vertmx (chem/module_vertmx_wrf.F) as chem/dry_dep_driver.F calls it for every transported species (WRF v4.8.0).\n\nThis is a COUPLING more than new physics, which is why it is short. WRF-Chem mixes every gas with the PBL scheme's HEAT eddy diffusivity -- `ekmfull(k) = max(1e-6, exch_h(k))`, with the two domain faces forced to zero -- and `exch_h` is exactly what components/atmospheric_dynamics/ysu/ysu.esm already computes and this repo already verifies to about 1e-7 (its variable K_h, 'WRF exch_hx; zero on the two domain faces'). The surface flux is the dry-deposition velocity from WRFWeselyDepositionVelocity. So the two halves of the chemistry column tendency that were already built meet here.\n\nTHE OPERATOR: dC/dt = (1/rho) d/dz ( rho K dC/dz ), with the diffusive flux through the ground replaced by the deposition loss rho(1) vd C(1) and the flux through the model top set to zero. It is written as that derivative and lowered by EarthSciDiscretizations' varcoeff_face_laplacian_lev_flux_bc, which turned out to be WRF's stencil exactly -- interface-valued coefficient with no face averaging, gradients over the layer-CENTRE spacing, and prescribed fluxes at both domain faces. Passing rho K rather than K as the coefficient, and dividing by rho once at the end, is what turns the rule's d/dz(K du/dz) into WRF's mass-weighted form.\n\nOne thing had to be checked rather than assumed: the rule builds its layer centres as (ze[k]+ze[k+1])/2, while WRF passes its own `zz` array from the geopotential. Measured on the dumped column they agree to 5.8e-8 relative, so the rule fires faithfully.\n\nWHAT WRF THROWS AWAY: vertmx is called over kts..kte, but dry_dep_driver.F writes the result back only for k = kts..kte-1. The TOP model layer's mixed value is computed and discarded, so the top layer never changes by vertical mixing. This component computes the tendency at every layer, including the top; a consumer reproducing WRF exactly must drop the top one.\n\nSPECIES AXIS (2026-11-12). The mixing ratio is shaped [lev, spc] -- one column per transported species on the axis `spc` (NSPEC, bound at the mount edge) -- while exch_h, the density and the geometry are shared, exactly as dry_dep_driver.F calls vertmx once per species with the same ekmfull. The derivative is the same derivative, now of a [lev, spc] field, and is lowered by EarthSciDiscretizations' varcoeff_face_laplacian_lev_flux_bc_tracer (the 1-D rule applied column by column, imported with rename tracer -> spc); vd and the two prescribed face fluxes are per species ([spc]). Column s of every result is exactly what the one-species form gave. This component's own tests use NSPEC = 10, the ten species of the kernel replays, in one test per call.\n\nThe tendency is exposed as an observed and the concentration is read algebraically -- this component does not own state that a consumer integrating the column will also drive."
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 59,
   "description": "Number of model layers, WRF's kte. 59 in the em_scm_xy reference column."
  },
  "NSPEC": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 10,
   "description": "Length of the species axis `spc`: the species this instance mixes. Bound at the mount edge by a consumer (every transported species of the mechanism); 10 in this component's own tests (so2, no2, no, o3, hno3, h2o2, hcho, nh3, co, csl, the ten species of the kernel replays)."
  }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "spc": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NSPEC"
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "ChemVerticalMixing": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d_tracer/rules/varcoeff_face_laplacian_lev_flux_bc_tracer.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV",
      "NTRACER": "NSPEC"
     },
     "rename": {
      "tracer": "spc"
     }
    }
   ],
   "subsystems": {
    "par": {
     "ref": "./vertmix_parameters.esm"
    }
   },
   "variables": {
    "C": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1e-6",
     "description": "Mixing ratio of each transported species on the axis, ppmV (WRF's chem array). Read algebraically, NOT owned: a consumer integrating the column drives it and adds this tendency to the chemical one (EqWeFiC CLAUDE.md, 'A component does not own state a consumer will also drive').",
     "shape": [
      "lev",
      "spc"
     ],
     "default": 0.01
    },
    "exch_h": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^2/s",
     "description": "Heat eddy diffusivity on the interfaces, WRF's exch_h -- which for this column IS the YSU scheme's K_h, already verified in this repo to ~1e-7 (components/atmospheric_dynamics/ysu/ysu.esm, variable K_h, 'WRF exch_hx; zero on the two domain faces'). WRF-Chem mixes every gas with the HEAT diffusivity, not a separate tracer one.",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "default": 1.0
    },
    "dryrho": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "description": "Dry air density at the layer centres, WRF's 1/alt.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "default": 1.0
    },
    "ze": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "Interface heights above the surface, WRF's zzfull = z_at_w(k) - z_at_w(kts).",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "default": 0.0
    },
    "vd": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "Dry-deposition velocity of each species on the axis, WRF's ddvel -- the CELL-AVERAGED value from WRFWeselyDepositionVelocity.vd, not the 2 m one.",
     "default": 0.0,
     "shape": [
      "spc"
     ]
    },
    "dz": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "Layer thickness (grid: column_cell_thickness).",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "zc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "Layer centre height (grid: column_cell_center). WRF passes its own `zz` here; measured against the dumped column, zz is the arithmetic mid-point of zzfull to 5.8e-8 relative, so the grid's derived centres are WRF's.",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ]
    },
    "k_turb": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^2/s",
     "description": "exch_h with WRF's treatment: floored at 1e-6 in the interior and forced to ZERO on the surface and model-top faces, so the only flux through the ground is deposition.",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "rho_w": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "description": "Dry air density on the interfaces, 0.5 (rho(i)+rho(i-1)) -- WRF's a_coeff.",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "K_rho": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/(m s)",
     "description": "The mass-weighted diffusivity rho K that the flux is built from. Passing rho K (rather than K) as the coefficient is what turns the EarthSciDiscretizations rule's d/dz(K du/dz) into WRF's (1/rho) d/dz(rho K du/dz).",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ]
    },
    "kdudz_bot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1e-6 kg/(m^2 s)",
     "description": "Prescribed diffusive flux through the SURFACE, per species: rho(1) vd[s] C(1,s), the dry-deposition loss. This is the free name the flux-BC rule reads.",
     "shape": [
      "spc"
     ]
    },
    "kdudz_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1e-6 kg/(m^2 s)",
     "description": "Prescribed flux through the MODEL TOP, per species: zero, because WRF sets ekmfull(kte+1) = 0.",
     "shape": [
      "spc"
     ]
    },
    "flux_div": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1e-6 kg/(m^3 s)",
     "description": "Divergence of the mass-weighted diffusive flux.",
     "shape": [
      "lev",
      "spc"
     ]
    },
    "dC_dt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1e-6/s",
     "description": "Tendency of the mixing ratio from vertical mixing plus dry deposition, ppmV/s. This is what a consumer integrating the chemistry column ADDS to the RADM2 chemical tendency.",
     "shape": [
      "lev",
      "spc"
     ]
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "dz",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "column_cell_thickness",
      "bindings": {
       "ze": "ze"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "zc",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "column_cell_center",
      "bindings": {
       "ze": "ze"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "k_turb",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "i"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "i": {
        "from": "lev_nodes"
       }
      },
      "args": [
       "exch_h"
      ],
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "i",
          1
         ]
        },
        0,
        {
         "op": "ifelse",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": ">=",
           "args": [
            "i",
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              "NLEV",
              1
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          0,
          {
           "op": "max",
           "args": [
            "par.k_floor",
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "exch_h",
              "i"
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "rho_w",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "i"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "i": {
        "from": "lev_nodes"
       }
      },
      "args": [
       "dryrho"
      ],
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "i",
          1
         ]
        },
        0,
        {
         "op": "ifelse",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": ">",
           "args": [
            "i",
            "NLEV"
           ]
          },
          0,
          {
           "op": "*",
           "args": [
            0.5,
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              {
               "op": "index",
               "args": [
                "dryrho",
                "i"
               ]
              },
              {
               "op": "index",
               "args": [
                "dryrho",
                {
                 "op": "-",
                 "args": [
                  "i",
                  1
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "K_rho",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "rho_w",
       "k_turb"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "kdudz_bot",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "s"
      ],
      "args": [],
      "ranges": {
       "s": {
        "from": "spc"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "dryrho",
          1
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "vd",
          "s"
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "C",
          1,
          "s"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "kdudz_top",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "s"
      ],
      "args": [],
      "ranges": {
       "s": {
        "from": "spc"
       }
      },
      "expr": 0
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "flux_div",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "K_rho",
         {
          "op": "D",
          "args": [
           "C"
          ],
          "wrt": "lev"
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "wrt": "lev"
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "dC_dt",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "k",
       "s"
      ],
      "args": [],
      "ranges": {
       "k": {
        "from": "lev"
       },
       "s": {
        "from": "spc"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "/",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "flux_div",
          "k",
          "s"
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "dryrho",
          "k"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "chem_vertmix_call60",
     "description": "Reference: a real64 replay of WRF's own SUBROUTINE vertmx (chem/module_vertmx_wrf.F, 201 lines and no dependencies) compiled with -fdefault-real-8 and driven at dt = 1e-3 s, so that (phi_out - phi_in)/dt IS the instantaneous tendency rather than the theta-weighted implicit step WRF takes at dt = 60 s. Driver and inputs: data/eqwefic/vertmx_kernel. The column state is the in-model dump data/eqwefic/dumps/chem_vertmx/esm_dump_chem_vertmx_60.json from the WRF-Chem 4.8 em_scm_xy run with chem_opt = 101 and gas_drydep_opt = 1 (data/eqwefic/chem_scm_dep), column i = its, j = jts, call 60; all ten species of the kernel replay on the axis, in the order so2, no2, no, o3, hno3, h2o2, hcho, nh3, co, csl.\nWHY A KERNEL DRIVER AND NOT THE IN-MODEL DUMP: WRF is real32, and at a dt small enough for the implicit step to approximate a rate the change in a mixing ratio is one or two ulps. Measured on this column, the in-model dt = 0.01 s replay gives 1-4 ulps for most species and exactly zero for CO. The dt ladder 0.5/2/8/32 s that was dumped alongside is resolved but carries the scheme's own O(dt) error; it agrees with this component to about 1 percent and is kept as a cross-check rather than as the reference. Tolerance: rel 1e-3 at every level of every species, with an absolute floor of 1e-3 times that species' largest |tendency| in the column (the per-species form of the relative L2 bound of 1e-3 the one-species tests carried; the floor is what keeps the float64-rounding-noise levels, where the tendency is 1e-16 of the peak, from being asserted to three digits), and rel 1e-3 with abs 1e-30 at the three levels of largest tendency of each species, unchanged; the operator was verified against this kernel at 1e-7 or better for every species whose tendency is above its own float64 rounding.",
