    {
     "id": "chem_vertmix_call1410",
     "description": "Reference: a real64 replay of WRF's own SUBROUTINE vertmx (chem/module_vertmx_wrf.F, 201 lines and no dependencies) compiled with -fdefault-real-8 and driven at dt = 1e-3 s, so that (phi_out - phi_in)/dt IS the instantaneous tendency rather than the theta-weighted implicit step WRF takes at dt = 60 s. Driver and inputs: data/eqwefic/vertmx_kernel. The column state is the in-model dump data/eqwefic/dumps/chem_vertmx/esm_dump_chem_vertmx_1410.json from the WRF-Chem 4.8 em_scm_xy run with chem_opt = 101 and gas_drydep_opt = 1 (data/eqwefic/chem_scm_dep), column i = its, j = jts, call 1410; all ten species of the kernel replay on the axis, in the order so2, no2, no, o3, hno3, h2o2, hcho, nh3, co, csl.\nWHY A KERNEL DRIVER AND NOT THE IN-MODEL DUMP: WRF is real32, and at a dt small enough for the implicit step to approximate a rate the change in a mixing ratio is one or two ulps. Measured on this column, the in-model dt = 0.01 s replay gives 1-4 ulps for most species and exactly zero for CO. The dt ladder 0.5/2/8/32 s that was dumped alongside is resolved but carries the scheme's own O(dt) error; it agrees with this component to about 1 percent and is kept as a cross-check rather than as the reference. Tolerance: rel 1e-3 at every level of every species, with an absolute floor of 1e-3 times that species' largest |tendency| in the column (the per-species form of the relative L2 bound of 1e-3 the one-species tests carried; the floor is what keeps the float64-rounding-noise levels, where the tendency is 1e-16 of the peak, from being asserted to three digits), and rel 1e-3 with abs 1e-30 at the three levels of largest tendency of each species, unchanged; the operator was verified against this kernel at 1e-7 or better for every species whose tendency is above its own float64 rounding.",
